{"commit": "1209e823b633c7ac73ae686896382b7207a907ac", "id": "1209e823b633c7ac73ae686896382b7207a907ac-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/bodil/im-rs", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T001910Z-ee273f1a", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/1209e823b633c7ac73ae686896382b7207a907ac-1/20260924T001910Z-ee273f1a/origin.json": "205d9afe6156a548fff3f813a9eaf8e578ceca4aadb5a183de5549d4aa98d672", "evidence/1209e823b633c7ac73ae686896382b7207a907ac-1/20260924T001910Z-ee273f1a/proposal.json": "899e3dde5f3fe69f207cdb58b6339597071cfd5fd549095530035ddd8033751c"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "im-rs", "status": "blocked", "subject": "RRB size table: don't pop conditional on cfg(debug_assertions)", "summary": "The `Size::Table` left-pop path put the side-effectful `size_table.pop_front()` call inside a `debug_assert_eq!`. In release builds the entire macro body was compiled out, so the size table never shrank, and later random-access indexing after `pop_front` read stale entries and panicked. The fix hoists the pop above the debug-only assertion.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:19:10.287169+00:00"}
